    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 the acceptance test is the only test class, and it passes along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS` (so compilation and MapStruct code generation succeeded).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of the `registrationDate` year) as a **derived** field, exactly as the test documents (\"derived from the owner's own fields, so seed-independent\").\n\nTwo files touched, no changes to the large `Owner` entity or the create pipeline:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema (generates the DTO field at build time).\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"membershipNumber\", expression = \"java(membershipNumber(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a small null-safe `default` helper that formats `customerCode + \"-M\" + %02d(year % 100)`. This mirrors the existing `displayName`/`initials` derivation pattern.\n\nWhy this keeps structural impact low: both `customerCode` and `registrationDate` are already persisted, so the membership number needs no new column, no new pipeline step/YAML, and no edit to the high-complexity `Owner` class. The only functions changed live in the tiny `OwnerMapper` interface (low `WMC_other`), and the null-guard keeps existing seed-owner serializations (which may lack a customer code or registration date) safe from NPEs.",
